<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lebou people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lebu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lebou are a people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> living mainly on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cap-vert">Cap-Vert</a> peninsula around Dakar, closely related to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> in language. Traditionally fishermen and farmers, they won independence from the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayor">Cayor</a> in the 1790s and governed themselves through elected leaders and councils until French rule. They remain a recognised community in Dakar, with their own traditional authorities and the Ndëpp healing rites.</p></div>
